-- emit: a chain of 24 functions, each passing its own parameter on to the
-- next (research 52, E1). `main` calls `f1 7`, so every `x` is `7` and every
-- test `x * 3 > 1000` is `false`. Fact 1 runs from caller to callee, and the
-- sweeps walked the program in the order it is written, callee first, so
-- each level of the chain cost a sweep; 24 levels reached the cap of 24
-- sweeps, and a round that did not converge rewrote nothing. The combined
-- solver (`backend.md` §9, *The combined solver*, slice 4) has no sweep to
-- run out of: every parameter is `7`, every test folds and every `x` goes,
-- down to `c=()=>216`. What stays is each call: nothing yet writes a call
-- whose result is known as that result (*Calls with known results*, 8a).
import Node exposing (Program)


f1 : Int → Int
f1 x =
    if x * 3 > 1000 then
        x
    else
        f2 x * 2 + f2 x


f2 : Int → Int
f2 x =
    if x * 3 > 1000 then
        x
    else
        f3 x * 2 + f3 x


f3 : Int → Int
f3 x =
    if x * 3 > 1000 then
        x
    else
        f4 x * 2 + f4 x


